  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Aircraft Engine and Engine Parts Manufacturing obligations for FY2026 to date total $5B. The Department of Defense accounted for the bulk of that spending with $4.9B, while other agencies recorded much smaller totals such as Department of Homeland Security with $74M and Department of Commerce with $5.4M. Obligations fell 58.7% year over year. Federal buyers issued 7,879 awards with an average award size of $630K. Historical fiscal-year totals show swings across the last six years: FY21 was $7.3B, FY22 was $11.1B, FY23 was $13.7B, FY24 was $8.4B, and FY25 was $12B. Top vendors in FY2026 to date include RTX CORPORATION at $1.6B, GENERAL ELECTRIC COMPANY at $1.2B and $444M, and ROLLS-ROYCE CORPORATION at $723M. THE BOEING COMPANY and LOCKHEED MARTIN CORPORATION also appear on the top list with entries at $283M, $107M, $133M, and $29.4M. Current-year totals are partial and represent fiscal year to date obligations only.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who is driving spending in NAICS 336412?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is driving spending, obligating $4.9B in FY2026 to date. Department of Homeland Security follows at $74M, with Department of Commerce at $5.4M and Department of Justice at $2.4M. Several agencies recorded much smaller obligations, including Department of State at $0."
      },
